WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:10.110
I'm tied to a tree, I don't know where I am, without a map, without internet.

2
00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.910
You're surely wondering how I ended up here.

3
00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:15.330
I'm always bragging to my wife that I have an incredible sense of direction,

4
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.610
that I'm sure I can't get lost.

5
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.390
So we set up this experiment.

6
00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.130
She'll take me wherever she wants,

7
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:26.250
and I have to get home without a map, internet and without anyone's help.

8
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.790
On top of that she said she's prepared something for me:

9
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:33.130
whether I succeed or not, in the end this thing will leave me speechless.

10
00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:36.950
Welcome to the first episode of "Get Home Without Help."

11
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.940
This will be the best day of my life.

12
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.220
Because I'm going to have a blast.

13
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.640
We found where we'll leave him.

14
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.120
I don't know how he'll manage, honestly, we've never been here.

15
00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:56.880
It'll be here.

16
00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.180
I decided not to show you where I am,

17
00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.300
so that you experience this adventure from my point of view.

18
00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:13.420
We look fine, right?

19
00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.550
Bravo, we are going dark.

20
00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:43.410
Sorry.

21
00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.070
What will people think when they see?

22
00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:58.330
Hi, people.

23
00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:00.370
By car it takes 34 minutes.

24
00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:07.670
If you'd left me there, I wouldn't have known which way to go to begin with.

25
00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.770
Oh, I didn't remember where the sun was.

26
00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:12.410
No, where's west?

27
00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:16.230
If I move for more than half an hour, I'm either eating or dead.

28
00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:16.870
Okay.

29
00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.960
I'd never have come back from there in my life.

30
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.320
I'm only afraid some dogs will attack you.

31
00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.540
Your free guess: where am I taking you?

32
00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.000
I didn't feel any climb.

33
00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.320
That is, I'm sitting in the car and didn't feel it going up and down.

34
00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.300
So I'm praying to God that it's in Vojvodina.

35
00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.200
I didn't hear anything like the sound of a bridge.

36
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:44.260
So I roughly know that we're between the Sava and the Danube, to the north.

37
00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.940
I haven't heard any human sounds for the last 15 minutes.

38
00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.230
Bro, I'm scared, bro.

39
00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.510
And you know what's worst — it suddenly got dark.

40
00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.410
Don't, people.

41
00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:06.110
Please don't, I beg you.

42
00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.070
Aha, observation, filming and access prohibited.

43
00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:14.770
Oh my god.

44
00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:15.870
What the fuck, where did you drive into?

45
00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:16.910
Hunting grounds.

46
00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.290
I don't know what this is.

47
00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:25.990
Close it, close it.

48
00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.110
Close it, close it, close it.

49
00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:34.730
Oh my god.

50
00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.480
Where did you bring me?

51
00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:44.880
Oh my god.

52
00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.460
Don't, stay, I beg you.

53
00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:49.740
Let's go, bye.

54
00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.420
Don't leave, I beg you.

55
00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.960
Where am I? What is this?

56
00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.020
What is this, bro?

57
00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.200
Okay, not a catastrophe.

58
00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.560
Everything is flat, which means I'm still in Vojvodina.

59
00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.500
Oh, this... look, a bike in these bushes.

60
00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.640
Hopefully it doesn't get punctured on these roses, damn.

61
00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.750
So, I have a bike, it'll be much easier.

62
00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:51.890
Now the big question: do I go left or right?

63
00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.530
I assume they didn't come by car from here, there are no tracks.

64
00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.770
But here I see that a car drove a little way.

65
00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.490
So I think I'll choose this direction.

66
00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.750
It's going to be a long, long day.

67
00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:21.430
Bro, this is much harder than I thought.

68
00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.290
Like I see they went that way, but it seems to me...

69
00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:29.090
Something tells me they went that way just to confuse me.

70
00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:30.150
Let's go.

71
00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.080
So they were here too.

72
00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:41.680
Good.

73
00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.980
So they're still going in this other direction.

74
00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:48.600
This is awesome.

75
00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.020
I need to raise the seat higher.

76
00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.540
I filmed one video with Aleksandar Roman, about cycling.

77
00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:55.960
We never finished that video.

78
00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.380
But I learned a lot while we were filming it.

79
00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:02.420
And one of the things — you should almost straighten your leg when you pedal.

80
00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:06.260
Which means I need to raise this like so.

81
00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:09.440
I think it'll be better like this.

82
00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:14.260
All right.

83
00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:15.880
Wow, how much easier it is to pedal.

84
00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:19.880
Excuse me, which way is Belgrade?

85
00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.840
I'm convinced we came from that side, I don't know why.

86
00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.060
If I go in the wrong direction and ride for an hour,

87
00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:30.840
I'll have lost two hours, because I'll have to come back.

88
00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.480
This street seems really lively to me.

89
00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.380
And now I don't know which direction Belgrade could be in.

90
00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.840
Honestly, I planned to get to the river,

91
00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.240
and there figure out whether it's the Sava or the Danube, and automatically understand where Belgrade is.

92
00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:48.280
Subconsciously I want to take out my phone and see where I am.

93
00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.600
Like okay, where do I go from here?

94
00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:52.240
I'm so dependent on these Google Maps.

95
00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.460
I mean I'm so lost, bro.

96
00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.480
I thought this would be much easier.

97
00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.220
For some reason I feel like going that way, I don't know why.

98
00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:01.200
I have a feeling there's a river there.

99
00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:03.040
I think it's time to trust my intuition.

100
00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:05.060
There's no point in going toward the field.

101
00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:08.560
But my heart tells me that I'll find the Sava there.

102
00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:09.240
I'm convinced.

103
00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.520
I don't know why I'm convinced.

104
00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:13.780
No sense at all, but we're riding into the field, bro, I don't care.

105
00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:17.080
This is one of the dumbest video ideas I've ever had.

106
00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:32.180
Anyway, I still think the river is in that direction.

107
00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:47.000
Incredibly, I don't know where Obrenovac is.

108
00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:48.860
I've heard about Obrenovac a million times.

109
00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:50.620
I know jokes about Obrenovac.

110
00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:51.700
But where it is — I don't know.

111
00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:54.080
I have no idea how it's situated relative to

112
00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:54.900
Belgrade.

113
00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.420
The plates I see are KS.

114
00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.580
What is KS, bro?

115
00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:01.080
I don't know, I don't know, really.

116
00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:01.700
Thank you.

117
00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:04.580
You're welcome.

118
00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:09.460
Imagine, people stop in a car and ask me for directions.

119
00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:12.220
I'll die, I can't be any more lost.

120
00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:13.940
Is this even real, seriously?

121
00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:17.060
At the second intersection people ask me where some place is.

122
00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:20.020
Anyway, I'm riding that way, even if I die, I'm riding to the end.

123
00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.300
Even though I know Belgrade is somewhere over there,

124
00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:24.460
I'm riding to the end this way.

125
00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:25.260
Never mind.

126
00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.000
There was a tracker in my bag,

127
00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:30.100
and Goca could check at any moment where I was.

128
00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:34.100
No! Dario messed up.

129
00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.820
He went toward Obrenovac.

130
00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.980
Down some road into the fields.

131
00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:39.500
And he should have gone here.

132
00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:40.860
And he went here.

133
00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:49.070
If he messed up at the very first turn, he'll never get home.

134
00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:51.990
Literally the first turn that could be missed, he missed.

135
00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.410
He'll never get home.

136
00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:55.670
You know what I haven't done in a long time?

137
00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:57.130
Ride a bike with no hands.

138
00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:21.800
I don't know, this road started to turn

139
00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:23.240
in a direction I don't want to go.

140
00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:24.940
I'm pedaling, bro, I'm dead, I don't feel well.

141
00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:26.960
My plan is this: I see some factory very far away.

142
00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:28.880
The factory is very far.

143
00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:30.880
But I have a feeling it's by the river.

144
00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:34.360
I'm riding to it, and there I'll find the river.

145
00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:35.960
And that's it. I've solved the whole puzzle.

146
00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:37.740
But if this factory isn't by the river,

147
00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.060
I've lost too much time.

148
00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:58.750
Too bad I didn't bring the drone,

149
00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.170
to film me pedaling.

150
00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:02.050
That would have been cheating, because I could have taken off

151
00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:02.910
and seen everything around.

152
00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:05.830
I'm very glad I did this.

153
00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:07.350
A real adventure.

154
00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.040
Left is Obrenovac, right is Progar.

155
00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:13.700
And I want to go straight.

156
00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:15.660
I'm ashamed, I really don't know where Obrenovac

157
00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:16.700
is on the map.

158
00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.020
You probably think I'm lying.

159
00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.200
But I swear, I don't know.

160
00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.460
But since I can't go straight, I'll go toward Obrenovac after all.

161
00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.360
And I don't see that factory, I don't know where it is.

162
00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:27.800
Is this forbidden or allowed?

163
00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:28.780
I'm very confused.

164
00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:34.610
Weak radiation.

165
00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:41.610
What the fuck.

166
00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:42.790
This is very bad.

167
00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.970
I turned this way to find the river.

168
00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:47.050
And found a lake.

169
00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:48.270
Where did a lake come from here?

170
00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.670
The lake isn't visible on the camera.

171
00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:52.830
I need to find some way to approach.

172
00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:53.890
This makes no sense at all.

173
00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:54.850
Where's the lake from, bro?

174
00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:55.950
This makes no sense at all.

175
00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:57.170
The Sava should be here,

176
00:10:57.530 --> 00:10:58.170
not a lake.

177
00:10:58.430 --> 00:10:59.550
Where is there a lake near Belgrade?

178
00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:00.530
I have no idea at all.

179
00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:03.650
We understood from the map that he made a big mistake

180
00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.770
and keeps making it further.

181
00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:07.390
And I don't know.

182
00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:08.450
I feel very sorry for him.

183
00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:10.910
I think at some point I'll go after him by car,

184
00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:11.810
because I feel very sorry for him.

185
00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:15.130
Everything went worse than I thought.

186
00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:17.070
What is this?

187
00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.740
So, I'm not one hundred percent sure it's a lake.

188
00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.260
I have a feeling the water is moving in one direction.

189
00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:42.840
When I look at the surface of the water, it seems to flow this way.

190
00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.100
But it looks like a lake,

191
00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:45.560
because over there I see one edge of the lake,

192
00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.340
and over there I see the other edge of the lake.

193
00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:51.120
If the river doesn't turn up to my right, then it's a lake.

194
00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:52.420
And where did a lake come from here?

195
00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:54.620
No idea.

196
00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:56.460
And I don't see that factory anywhere anymore, folks.

197
00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:58.860
I see it.

198
00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:04.840
It's still very far.

199
00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:06.240
I still want to get to it.

200
00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:10.740
Dario reached the lake and now can ride here

201
00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:12.440
to get back onto that normal road.

202
00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:13.640
But I don't know what he'll do.

203
00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.060
There he is, he's at the lake.

204
00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:16.500
Now that I've gone down to the water,

205
00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.700
it'll be interesting: I'm climbing uphill again.

206
00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.440
Only sweat is pouring into my eyes and stinging.

207
00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:29.400
Oh, the dogs ruined everything for me.

208
00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:39.020
I don't know why I feel like it's only just begun,

209
00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.700
and I thought I was somewhere halfway.

210
00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:47.740
I swallowed a gnat.

211
00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:49.960
Honestly, at this moment I have no idea what I'm doing.

212
00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:50.760
Just pedaling.

213
00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:52.820
I think it's a very, very dumb idea.

214
00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.140
I have no idea at all which way I'm going.

215
00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:56.900
I thought I'd reach the Sava River.

216
00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:58.220
And reached some lake.

217
00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.140
There, now I'm in a populated place.

218
00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:02.300
There was no sign at the entrance, I don't know what it's called.

219
00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.500
I want to find some store, eat a chocolate bar,

220
00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:06.180
sweeten up a little and rest a little,

221
00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:08.000
because I'm hungry and have been riding for a very long time.

222
00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:17.160
I'm still coughing because of that gnat that flew into my throat.

223
00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:24.960
I found a gas station called "Art Pumpa."

224
00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:28.020
What's the connection between art and gasoline?

225
00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:05.900
This is one of the coolest days of my life.

226
00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:08.200
Don't be surprised if this turns into a series.

227
00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:10.340
I have a feeling I'm about to run into the Sava.

228
00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.140
That lake only confused me.

229
00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:25.080
This is definitely not the Sava.

230
00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:27.580
It can't be the Sava.

231
00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:29.580
What's this forest doing here, bro?

232
00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.140
I'm very curious to ride into the forest.

233
00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:34.840
The Aleksandar Roman in me wants to do a bit of off-roading.

234
00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:36.320
Let's try, see what it costs us.

235
00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:38.220
A little time and energy.

236
00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:40.020
This leads nowhere.

237
00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:42.460
Aleksandar Roman would have ridden to the end.

238
00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:44.620
It's just possible that beyond this forest is the Sava.

239
00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:46.040
Right there, the Sava.

240
00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:49.040
This was the first time I felt I really don't understand what I'm doing.

241
00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:51.300
But I decided to believe in myself anyway,

242
00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:53.440
to believe in this crazy intuition.

243
00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:56.440
Something in me says this is the direction to the Sava.

244
00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:58.140
Will some hunters shoot me in the forest?

245
00:14:58.220 --> 00:14:59.340
Thinking I'm a wild boar.

246
00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:03.540
It's fenced here.

247
00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:05.880
Why is it fenced?

248
00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:07.280
I'm a complete idiot.

249
00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:12.370
The Sava is there, one hundred percent.

250
00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:13.130
They fenced it off.

251
00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:13.930
Let's go left.

252
00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.230
My intuition

253
00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:24.570
hasn't been right so far.

254
00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.450
But it hasn't been wrong either.

255
00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:27.770
So...

256
00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.540
Bro, what is this?

257
00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:40.740
What an

258
00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:41.400
idiot I am.

259
00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:43.320
Unheard-of fool.

260
00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:45.540
How did I manage to get stuck in this forest?

261
00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:49.680
Never in my life will I turn into a forest again.

262
00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:52.500
I just want to add that I never ride a bike at all.

263
00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:56.640
The last time I rode was when I filmed that cycling video that I didn't finish.

264
00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:59.080
And before that who knows when I last rode.

265
00:15:59.340 --> 00:16:00.060
Oh, my butt.

266
00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:03.580
A person can't get through here on a bike.

267
00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:07.820
Aleksandar Roman.

268
00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:10.960
The strongest cyclist in Serbia and beyond.

269
00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:12.620
Unstoppable biker.

270
00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:14.040
Off-roader.

271
00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:15.720
Unstoppable force.

272
00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:19.140
I hear a car.

273
00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:20.480
I hear a car.

274
00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:20.960
Yes.

275
00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:22.260
Yes.

276
00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:23.620
End of the forest.

277
00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:25.480
Oh my god.

278
00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:31.910
Yes.

279
00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:34.650
I have no idea what road this is.

280
00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:37.330
But I'm convinced the Sava is there.

281
00:16:37.670 --> 00:16:38.490
This is a dam,

282
00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:40.790
so the river doesn't flood here.

283
00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:43.190
It's the only thing in this life that makes sense.

284
00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:44.510
I'm going straight.

285
00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:45.150
Not going left.

286
00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:45.810
Not going right.

287
00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:46.930
Not following the road.

288
00:16:47.010 --> 00:16:47.610
But going straight.

289
00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:50.210
Please, let my intuition have been right all this time.

290
00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:51.850
Even the forest didn't stop me.

291
00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:52.590
There.

292
00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:54.490
It must be this cool, huh?

293
00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:58.770
There it is.

294
00:16:59.230 --> 00:16:59.830
The Sava.

295
00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:01.870
Oh, that's not the Sava.

296
00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:07.610
What is this?

297
00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:09.750
What is this?

298
00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:11.690
Where's the Sava?

299
00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:11.710
What?

300
00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:34.680
I still have that drop of hope.

301
00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:35.880
That is, I haven't given up.

302
00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:38.540
And if I give up, then what?

303
00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:40.740
I'll just take a break, and then I'll have to ride again.

304
00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:42.080
So giving up isn't an option for me.

305
00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:44.520
My intuition hasn't been wrong yet.

306
00:17:44.740 --> 00:17:45.940
But it hasn't been accurate either.

307
00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:47.440
Oh, there are too many mosquitoes here, folks.

308
00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:51.100
And I don't need anything for motivation.

309
00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:53.020
I only need mosquitoes to chase me away.

310
00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:54.620
I'm still convinced the Sava is there.

311
00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:58.720
And I'll only pray that at some point I see the Sava on the right.

312
00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:01.440
I'm an idiot.

313
00:18:02.320 --> 00:18:03.460
I have no time to wait.

314
00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.820
Just, please, be on this side.

315
00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:13.800
Oh, folks, look.

316
00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:15.960
The road leads to the Sava.

317
00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:17.480
If the Sava is there.

318
00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:21.460
Anyway, the Sava is there, 100%.

319
00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:23.400
I'm riding into the forest again.

320
00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.760
I did say I wouldn't ride into the forest.

321
00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:27.540
Sava, please, Sava, show up.

322
00:19:26.400 --> 00:19:27.440
I still have strength.

323
00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.000
Bro, this bike has served me well.

324
00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:31.280
It's really good.

325
00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:32.280
Let's go.

326
00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:44.800
Along the Sava I reached a dead end.

327
00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:46.300
That is, I can't go any further.

328
00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:48.960
So the plan is to climb the hill by the river.

329
00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.500
I think then I'll just ride along this hill

330
00:19:50.740 --> 00:19:51.560
to BG.

331
00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:53.540
I don't know how sure I am about this road.

332
00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.680
I think I'll take it anyway.

333
00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:58.400
Because I have a feeling it will get dark soon.

334
00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.240
I can't take breaks.

335
00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:03.360
That is, I have to pedal.

336
00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:04.720
Around me there's peace, silence.

337
00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:06.640
On one side the Sava.

338
00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:07.800
Really magical.

339
00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:09.860
Well, it would be magical if I weren't dead tired

340
00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:10.940
and if my butt didn't hurt.

341
00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.260
How my butt hurts, folks.

342
00:20:12.380 --> 00:20:14.740
I'm very glad I bought those cycling shorts.

343
00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:15.580
But, bro...

344
00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:18.220
I don't know what it would have been like without them.

345
00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:27.420
Anyway, I need to take a break.

346
00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:31.380
The problem is that the mosquitoes bite me as soon as I stop for 5 seconds.

347
00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:36.880
The worst isn't the aching muscles, well, in the thighs.

348
00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:39.820
What hurts the most is my butt and my wrists.

349
00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:42.140
Hands, because I lean on the handlebars.

350
00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:46.840
And my back a little, because I've been bent over for a very long time.

351
00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:49.120
Although the fact that I found the river is very good.

352
00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:51.020
I mean, I know exactly where I am and where to go.

353
00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:52.600
On the other hand, bro,

354
00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:54.380
these mosquitoes killed me.

355
00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:55.320
Killed me.

356
00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.200
I can't take breaks, you understand?

357
00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:03.920
Here, bro, I stop — and 20 mosquitoes attack me.

358
00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:05.740
It's not that I've run out of stamina,

359
00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:08.780
I'm just not used to riding a bike for so long.

360
00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:11.760
My joints hurt and my back.

361
00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:20.960
Wow.

362
00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:23.500
It would be nicer if I were on a quad bike.

363
00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:25.960
But okay, a bike is fine too.

364
00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:27.620
Behind me is a motorway.

365
00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:33.480
In my head, in front of me there should be New Belgrade,

366
00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:34.360
not a motorway.

367
00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.980
This is the road to Belgrade.

368
00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:42.760
And over there is the road to Zagreb.

369
00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:44.620
Where did they leave me, bro?

370
00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:49.320
Anyway, I'm convinced this is the road to Belgrade.

371
00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:51.260
It's just that then it's possible the Sava winds so much

372
00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:52.760
and that I misunderstood something here.

373
00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:56.940
There it is, the motorway. A wonderful sight.

374
00:21:57.220 --> 00:21:59.220
And the Sava and the Danube merge in Belgrade.

375
00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:00.420
Where am I, bro?

376
00:22:00.560 --> 00:22:02.260
I'm following the course of the Sava.

377
00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:04.960
Belgrade is nowhere. Where did they dump me, bro?

378
00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:09.920
This is taking too long, bro.

379
00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:12.060
I, folks, have been pedaling for hours.

380
00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:13.300
I can't pedal anymore.

381
00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:14.680
This is a bumpy road.

382
00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:17.320
My joints have fallen off. My butt has fallen off.

383
00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:19.280
I can't anymore, folks. Where is Belgrade?

384
00:22:21.420 --> 00:22:23.520
Where does this motorway come from? What is this, bro?

385
00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:25.320
Where have I ended up?

386
00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:27.920
It's funny, but I have no choice. I have to get home.

387
00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:30.160
My joints have fallen off.

388
00:22:39.410 --> 00:22:40.970
Oh, at least the road isn't bumpy anymore.

389
00:22:44.030 --> 00:22:47.730
I have a feeling that riding on this smooth road is five times easier.

390
00:22:47.850 --> 00:22:50.890
However good that dirt road looked,

391
00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:52.270
riding on it is much harder.

392
00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:54.910
The worst thing is that I don't have a light on the bike

393
00:22:55.050 --> 00:22:55.750
that I rented.

394
00:22:55.950 --> 00:22:57.350
I'm not lit up at all.

395
00:22:57.550 --> 00:23:00.910
If I ride at night, I have to ride the same way, off-road, so there are no cars.

396
00:23:00.910 --> 00:23:03.490
I can't ride along the civilized route, that's very bad.

397
00:23:05.710 --> 00:23:06.830
The last chocolate bar.

398
00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:12.810
The sun has never set faster in my life.

399
00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:15.170
Damn it. I have two sips of water left.

400
00:23:18.710 --> 00:23:19.770
Oh, how thirsty I am.

401
00:23:19.990 --> 00:23:21.730
Anyway, I'm going in the right direction, 100%.

402
00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:23.570
But, bro, I don't know why it's so far.

403
00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:24.670
I've been pedaling for a very long time.

404
00:23:26.430 --> 00:23:26.990
Nothing.

405
00:23:31.540 --> 00:23:32.480
Good evening.

406
00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:38.190
Sooner or later this was bound to happen.

407
00:23:38.190 --> 00:23:41.210
How did I manage that?

408
00:23:45.370 --> 00:23:46.310
How is that even possible?

409
00:23:49.160 --> 00:23:49.360
Okay.

410
00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:52.000
It's been a long time since I put a chain back on, folks.

411
00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:58.030
It should be fairly simple.

412
00:24:08.610 --> 00:24:11.410
I think it's time to reveal the mystery of what's really going on

413
00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:12.610
and where I went wrong.

414
00:24:12.790 --> 00:24:15.610
Considering that I was convinced I was in this part,

415
00:24:15.610 --> 00:24:16.870
let's say, of Serbia,

416
00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:19.130
because I hadn't crossed any bridge over any river,

417
00:24:19.450 --> 00:24:21.330
I knew I had to run into a river,

418
00:24:21.330 --> 00:24:23.750
whether the Sava or the Danube.

419
00:24:23.850 --> 00:24:25.950
You understood from the video that I was chasing the Sava.

420
00:24:26.110 --> 00:24:27.590
And I really did find it.

421
00:24:27.690 --> 00:24:28.670
But there's one problem.

422
00:24:31.160 --> 00:24:32.200
The Sava winds.

423
00:24:32.560 --> 00:24:34.620
I was convinced the Sava was straight.

424
00:24:36.460 --> 00:24:38.500
Of course, I ended up on these bends of the Sava.

425
00:24:38.920 --> 00:24:41.320
And the route that should have already ended

426
00:24:41.320 --> 00:24:42.980
looked like it was only beginning.

427
00:24:43.120 --> 00:24:44.840
The bumpy roads were killing me.

428
00:24:45.140 --> 00:24:46.480
I was riding twice as slowly.

429
00:24:46.940 --> 00:24:48.280
Fatigue was starting to catch up with me.

430
00:24:48.460 --> 00:24:50.140
But I knew I couldn't give up.

431
00:24:56.010 --> 00:24:57.370
Music helps me a lot.

432
00:24:57.590 --> 00:24:59.570
I don't know why I didn't start listening earlier.

433
00:25:03.630 --> 00:25:10.760
This will sound silly.

434
00:25:21.870 --> 00:25:23.890
But literally the last two hours

435
00:25:23.990 --> 00:25:25.470
I've been constantly thinking about giving up.

436
00:25:28.150 --> 00:25:29.350
And I keep thinking to myself —

437
00:25:29.530 --> 00:25:30.950
this will be a bit silly, but like —

438
00:25:31.030 --> 00:25:33.090
what if some cycling professional

439
00:25:33.090 --> 00:25:34.610
or, say, Aleksandar,

440
00:25:34.670 --> 00:25:35.870
whom I mentioned,

441
00:25:35.930 --> 00:25:36.970
what if he watches this video?

442
00:25:37.290 --> 00:25:39.150
And I want that when he watches the video, he says:

443
00:25:39.410 --> 00:25:39.770
bro,

444
00:25:41.410 --> 00:25:42.610
the guy had never ridden a bike,

445
00:25:42.730 --> 00:25:44.010
and did it in one day.

446
00:25:44.130 --> 00:25:44.650
Like okay,

447
00:25:44.650 --> 00:25:45.630
well done, he tried,

448
00:25:45.730 --> 00:25:46.390
he gave it his all.

449
00:25:50.510 --> 00:25:51.430
I want them to be like:

450
00:25:51.710 --> 00:25:52.910
for an amateur he's really good.

451
00:25:53.010 --> 00:25:53.870
Like you can see the guy

452
00:25:54.110 --> 00:25:55.170
has some fire inside.

453
00:25:55.170 --> 00:25:56.530
And it's not that I need

454
00:25:56.570 --> 00:25:57.710
some kind of, like, their

455
00:25:57.890 --> 00:25:58.250
recognition,

456
00:25:58.330 --> 00:25:58.690
for them to say:

457
00:25:58.770 --> 00:25:59.690
hey, dude, good job.

458
00:25:59.790 --> 00:26:01.410
It's purely so that I myself know that, well...

459
00:26:01.510 --> 00:26:02.570
I don't know, it's hard to explain.

460
00:26:05.550 --> 00:26:06.930
I want to be one of those people

461
00:26:06.950 --> 00:26:08.410
who, you know, have a fire inside,

462
00:26:08.490 --> 00:26:09.930
who won't give up just like that.

463
00:26:10.030 --> 00:26:11.350
Even if there's no point in it at all.

464
00:26:16.350 --> 00:26:18.010
It's not the best use of my time,

465
00:26:18.250 --> 00:26:18.790
let's say.

466
00:26:18.850 --> 00:26:20.070
Like not the most profitable.

467
00:26:21.790 --> 00:26:23.250
The only person you're fighting is

468
00:26:23.330 --> 00:26:23.670
yourself.

469
00:26:23.830 --> 00:26:25.070
And it's good when you have

470
00:26:25.330 --> 00:26:26.310
a good opinion of yourself,

471
00:26:26.390 --> 00:26:27.330
when you believe in yourself.

472
00:26:27.450 --> 00:26:28.990
Someday, when things are really hard for you,

473
00:26:29.070 --> 00:26:30.410
and you'll have to push on,

474
00:26:30.510 --> 00:26:31.930
when you'll have to give it your all —

475
00:26:32.190 --> 00:26:32.550
you'll be able to.

476
00:26:33.110 --> 00:26:35.010
Because you've done silly things like this, you understand?

477
00:26:35.430 --> 00:26:36.470
You do silly things like this,

478
00:26:36.530 --> 00:26:37.710
and you pulled those silly things off.

479
00:26:37.710 --> 00:26:39.790
Which means you can pull off what really matters to you.

480
00:26:39.930 --> 00:26:40.910
All this is just

481
00:26:42.170 --> 00:26:42.690
training.

482
00:26:44.330 --> 00:26:45.390
We keep pedaling.

483
00:26:45.550 --> 00:26:46.190
I'm thirsty.

484
00:26:46.350 --> 00:26:48.270
I'd drink water from a puddle right now, I swear.

485
00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:54.420
How bad can this water be?

486
00:26:55.220 --> 00:26:56.340
Really, it's just rain.

487
00:26:58.990 --> 00:27:00.790
Wait, I have two drops left here.

488
00:27:01.050 --> 00:27:02.250
Every drop is worth its weight in gold.

489
00:27:15.560 --> 00:27:16.860
And this one is for Bear Grylls.

490
00:27:33.490 --> 00:27:36.170
The guy looked at me like: what idiot is this?

491
00:27:38.530 --> 00:27:39.850
And today is Sunday.

492
00:27:39.910 --> 00:27:40.630
A day of rest.

493
00:27:40.770 --> 00:27:42.230
Please be good dogs.

494
00:27:42.370 --> 00:27:43.730
Please be good dogs.

495
00:27:43.810 --> 00:27:44.230
Hi, handsome.

496
00:27:44.770 --> 00:27:45.550
Do you want to be petted?

497
00:27:45.630 --> 00:27:46.290
Are you a good dog?

498
00:27:47.210 --> 00:27:48.170
Good boy, handsome.

499
00:27:48.610 --> 00:27:49.170
Bye, bye.

500
00:27:54.830 --> 00:27:55.750
Wow, how dangerous you are.

501
00:27:56.150 --> 00:27:57.210
Good, they didn't attack me.

502
00:28:00.160 --> 00:28:02.980
Just give me a better road already.

503
00:28:12.820 --> 00:28:14.120
I wished for a new road.

504
00:28:14.240 --> 00:28:15.440
I got a new road.

505
00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:16.420
Yes.

506
00:28:17.840 --> 00:28:18.480
Finally.

507
00:28:18.920 --> 00:28:19.560
Finally.

508
00:28:24.700 --> 00:28:25.340
Yes.

509
00:28:36.510 --> 00:28:37.330
As you can see,

510
00:28:37.610 --> 00:28:38.090
it's getting dark.

511
00:28:38.330 --> 00:28:39.730
I'm getting more and more tired.

512
00:28:39.870 --> 00:28:41.370
Anyway, it's really hard for me.

513
00:28:41.370 --> 00:28:43.090
I can't take a break, both because of the mosquitoes

514
00:28:43.190 --> 00:28:44.330
and because it will get dark.

515
00:28:44.490 --> 00:28:45.370
I have a plan B

516
00:28:45.610 --> 00:28:46.570
for situations like this.

517
00:28:46.630 --> 00:28:47.330
This plan...

518
00:28:58.360 --> 00:28:59.460
A higher gear.

519
00:29:00.360 --> 00:29:02.160
Low gears aren't for me.

520
00:29:57.160 --> 00:29:57.900
Come on, Belgrade already!

521
00:29:58.080 --> 00:29:59.200
I don't have much daylight left.

522
00:30:07.640 --> 00:30:10.820
I can't anymore, it's getting dark, I can't.

523
00:30:10.820 --> 00:30:12.480
Plan B was the worst plan so far.

524
00:30:13.520 --> 00:30:14.080
Definitely.

525
00:30:14.080 --> 00:30:15.200
I need to pull myself together,

526
00:30:15.500 --> 00:30:17.160
try to catch one rhythm,

527
00:30:17.160 --> 00:30:18.000
hold it

528
00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:19.440
and take as few breaks as possible.

529
00:30:19.440 --> 00:30:21.160
Because behind me it's already getting really dark.

530
00:30:21.160 --> 00:30:23.480
I see it getting darker and darker.

531
00:30:24.460 --> 00:30:25.960
But how beautiful it is, bro.

532
00:30:25.960 --> 00:30:27.220
How beautiful it is, bro.

533
00:30:32.200 --> 00:30:33.900
How somehow everything is beautiful.

534
00:30:33.900 --> 00:30:35.740
I don't know how to explain.

535
00:30:40.240 --> 00:30:41.600
It really looks magical.

536
00:30:41.600 --> 00:30:43.900
Wow, look at the sky behind.

537
00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:45.660
Wow, look at the sky behind.

538
00:30:45.660 --> 00:30:46.580
The sun is setting.

539
00:30:46.580 --> 00:30:48.920
I got a bit relaxed, bro.

540
00:30:48.920 --> 00:30:51.220
These bumpy roads are the worst.

541
00:30:52.700 --> 00:30:55.160
My joints and my butt hurt a lot.

542
00:30:57.470 --> 00:31:00.070
Bro, this sun is setting faster and faster.

543
00:31:08.420 --> 00:31:10.360
I got onto a slightly better road.

544
00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:12.440
Oh, how much better the road is.

545
00:31:12.980 --> 00:31:14.520
Oh, how I screwed up.

546
00:31:15.140 --> 00:31:16.760
Oh, how much better the road is.

547
00:31:16.760 --> 00:31:20.060
What an idiot I was to ride off-road along the Sava.

548
00:31:24.560 --> 00:31:25.820
Here's another motorway.

549
00:31:29.750 --> 00:31:30.970
I can't believe it.

550
00:31:31.590 --> 00:31:34.270
I can't believe what I just did to myself.

551
00:31:36.700 --> 00:31:38.120
I turned on the flash on my phone.

552
00:31:38.480 --> 00:31:39.460
When a car comes along,

553
00:31:39.460 --> 00:31:42.580
I wave like this so that he sees me and doesn't hit me.

554
00:31:42.580 --> 00:31:44.500
Bro, this is so stupid.

555
00:31:55.710 --> 00:31:57.030
I'm so thirsty.

556
00:31:57.630 --> 00:31:59.130
I'm so hungry.

557
00:31:59.130 --> 00:32:01.030
Pedaling non-stop.

558
00:32:01.030 --> 00:32:02.030
The road is good.

559
00:32:02.030 --> 00:32:03.530
But it's so dark.

560
00:32:03.530 --> 00:32:05.170
And every muscle hurts so much.

561
00:32:05.170 --> 00:32:06.190
My ankles,

562
00:32:06.190 --> 00:32:07.670
knees,

563
00:32:07.670 --> 00:32:08.250
thighs,

564
00:32:08.250 --> 00:32:09.070
butt hurt.

565
00:32:09.070 --> 00:32:11.170
Every part of my butt hurts.

566
00:32:11.170 --> 00:32:11.930
Shoulders.

567
00:32:11.930 --> 00:32:12.930
Upper back.

568
00:32:12.930 --> 00:32:13.850
Lower back.

569
00:32:13.850 --> 00:32:14.350
Neck.

570
00:32:14.350 --> 00:32:15.070
Head.

571
00:32:15.070 --> 00:32:17.790
These wrists are just killing me.

572
00:32:17.790 --> 00:32:19.010
It's very dark.

573
00:32:19.010 --> 00:32:21.110
I was afraid of being hit even during the day,

574
00:32:21.110 --> 00:32:22.230
let alone at night.

575
00:32:22.230 --> 00:32:23.390
On top of everything

576
00:32:23.390 --> 00:32:25.130
I'm extremely thirsty.

577
00:32:25.130 --> 00:32:26.390
I'm extremely hungry.

578
00:32:26.390 --> 00:32:27.190
I need a break.

579
00:32:27.190 --> 00:32:28.110
I haven't taken a break

580
00:32:28.110 --> 00:32:29.610
for I don't know how many of the last hours.

581
00:32:29.610 --> 00:32:30.970
I'm glad I'm in shape.

582
00:32:30.970 --> 00:32:32.890
My body is slowly starting to fail.

583
00:32:32.890 --> 00:32:36.330
The worst thing for me was that I didn't know how far I was from the city.

584
00:32:36.330 --> 00:32:37.810
Everything around me was black.

585
00:32:37.810 --> 00:32:39.830
I was hoping to see some building,

586
00:32:39.830 --> 00:32:40.930
some lights.

587
00:32:40.930 --> 00:32:42.310
Nothing was visible.

588
00:32:42.310 --> 00:32:44.190
I had a feeling that trees were surrounding me.

589
00:32:44.190 --> 00:32:45.830
Cars drove past.

590
00:32:45.830 --> 00:32:48.710
I only wanted to take a short break.

591
00:32:48.710 --> 00:32:50.090
Just to come to my senses a little.

592
00:32:51.150 --> 00:32:52.710
Folks, I found salvation.

593
00:32:52.710 --> 00:32:54.350
A café, bar and restaurant.

594
00:32:54.350 --> 00:32:55.210
That's exactly what I needed.

595
00:32:55.950 --> 00:32:57.130
I can't stand anymore.

596
00:32:57.130 --> 00:33:14.120
You can't see it, but this mask is soaked through.

597
00:33:16.260 --> 00:33:17.800
I'm literally done.

598
00:33:24.780 --> 00:33:25.260
Water.

599
00:33:35.690 --> 00:33:36.170
Dario!

600
00:33:37.650 --> 00:33:39.070
What are you doing, dude?

601
00:33:39.170 --> 00:33:41.610
Goca saw on the map that I had stopped moving.

602
00:33:41.610 --> 00:33:45.190
She got worried and came by car to see what was happening to me.

603
00:33:46.330 --> 00:33:47.790
Goca found me.

604
00:33:47.790 --> 00:33:49.850
I can't even be happy, my brain is working that poorly.

605
00:33:52.750 --> 00:33:54.410
Literally: I made it to this café,

606
00:33:56.490 --> 00:33:58.430
and that's where my plan ends.

607
00:33:58.430 --> 00:33:59.230
I don't know what to do next.

608
00:33:59.230 --> 00:34:00.730
My body has completely given out.

609
00:34:00.730 --> 00:34:02.230
My brain has completely given out.

610
00:34:02.230 --> 00:34:03.770
Night, I'll die.

611
00:34:04.370 --> 00:34:05.530
I need to come up with some plan.

612
00:34:05.530 --> 00:34:07.350
First have something to eat, and then you'll come up with some plan.

613
00:34:08.010 --> 00:34:09.170
How did you find me?

614
00:34:10.850 --> 00:34:12.490
I rode very little on the road.

615
00:34:12.490 --> 00:34:14.410
It was all dirt tracks.

616
00:34:15.270 --> 00:34:16.410
Looks appetizing.

617
00:34:16.410 --> 00:34:17.870
It smells really good.

618
00:34:17.870 --> 00:34:18.490
Really, really.

619
00:34:27.710 --> 00:34:28.790
Calories.

620
00:34:31.470 --> 00:34:32.990
Ever since I reached the Sava,

621
00:34:32.990 --> 00:34:34.630
I hadn't taken a break.

622
00:34:35.570 --> 00:34:36.270
Because of the mosquitoes.

623
00:34:37.450 --> 00:34:39.370
I stop — and the mosquitoes just devour me.

624
00:34:39.370 --> 00:34:41.390
I hadn't taken any breaks at all.

625
00:34:41.390 --> 00:34:44.390
After dinner we decided to load the bike into the car.

626
00:34:44.390 --> 00:34:45.750
This isn't the end of the story.

627
00:34:45.750 --> 00:34:47.210
Because just two minutes later

628
00:34:47.210 --> 00:34:49.070
I regretted my decision.

629
00:34:49.070 --> 00:34:52.830
I actually told Goca on purpose never to tell me where I am

630
00:34:52.830 --> 00:34:54.370
and how far I have left to the city.

631
00:34:54.370 --> 00:34:56.250
Only I didn't expect this.

632
00:34:56.250 --> 00:34:57.870
Bro, you're lying to me.

633
00:34:57.870 --> 00:34:59.110
We'll walk on foot just this far.

634
00:34:59.110 --> 00:34:59.550
Yes, yes.

635
00:35:00.390 --> 00:35:01.230
Oh my god.

636
00:35:01.230 --> 00:35:02.490
How close I was.

637
00:35:03.370 --> 00:35:05.870
You shouldn't have come for me, bro.

638
00:35:06.390 --> 00:35:08.210
You shouldn't have come for me.

639
00:35:08.210 --> 00:35:10.270
No, bro, no.

640
00:35:10.270 --> 00:35:12.690
I thought I still had two hours of riding.

641
00:35:12.690 --> 00:35:13.710
That's it.

642
00:35:15.750 --> 00:35:16.490
There it is, New Belgrade.

643
00:35:16.490 --> 00:35:18.670
That is, I had 20 minutes left at most.

644
00:35:18.670 --> 00:35:19.490
Stop.

645
00:35:24.910 --> 00:35:26.790
I gave up at the very end.

646
00:35:30.310 --> 00:35:32.170
Let's go back,

647
00:35:32.170 --> 00:35:33.910
and I'll ride home on the bike.

648
00:35:35.290 --> 00:35:35.950
Please.

649
00:35:35.950 --> 00:35:37.650
I feel like a complete loser.

650
00:35:37.650 --> 00:35:40.850
I tried so hard and failed at the very end.

651
00:35:40.850 --> 00:35:42.650
I can't lose in the last five percent.

652
00:35:49.510 --> 00:35:52.350
Such a surprise that it hit me right in the heart.

653
00:35:52.350 --> 00:35:54.830
My soul hurt so much that the next morning,

654
00:35:54.830 --> 00:35:56.850
the moment I opened my eyes, I got on the bike

655
00:35:56.850 --> 00:35:58.450
and rode the rest of the way.

656
00:36:00.230 --> 00:36:01.950
Here I am at the sign of the floating restaurant.

657
00:36:02.470 --> 00:36:03.670
Since I arrived very early,

658
00:36:03.670 --> 00:36:04.710
unfortunately it's not open.

659
00:36:08.990 --> 00:36:09.810
Believe it or not,

660
00:36:09.810 --> 00:36:11.370
now I feel even worse.

661
00:36:11.370 --> 00:36:12.590
Now I also have muscle soreness.

662
00:36:12.990 --> 00:36:14.230
Now I've cooled down.

663
00:36:14.230 --> 00:36:15.570
The pain is much stronger.

664
00:36:15.570 --> 00:36:16.630
The only thing — I'm more rested,

665
00:36:16.630 --> 00:36:17.970
but everything hurts twice as much.

666
00:36:17.970 --> 00:36:19.750
Now all that's left is to return the bike,

667
00:36:19.750 --> 00:36:20.930
and then I'll show you

668
00:36:20.930 --> 00:36:23.290
what Goca prepared for me last night.

669
00:36:26.950 --> 00:36:30.010
It stung me so much that I literally opened my eyes and came here.